They must die, sadly. However, there are ways to kill enemies without
taking the murder penalty, or to delay their deaths until it's more
convenient.

1. Polymorph them, because murder = killing peaceful *human*
This wastes vital polymorph zaps. I usually do this to the Minetown
priest instead. If he polymorphs into a non shock-resistant monster,
he can easily die to his *own deity's lightning bolts*.

2. Feed them to a buff pet.
BUURRRRP. Most anything stronger than your puppy can kill them.

3. Conflict.
If all the watchmen are mad at you, hide in a boulder fort and wait
until you're surrounded, or use some *other* strategy to lead them
into the same space.
Put on a ring of conflict and they'll smash each other to bits.
Unfortunately, you run the risk of getting blasted with attack wands.

4. Dig a hole.
Dig a hole at a chokepoint near the downstair, preferably *after*
having grabbed the luckstone. Jump down the hole, come back upstairs,
and watch the minetown watch fall down the hole into the next level.
When they're all gone, dig a retreat or teleport to the other side of
the hole.
This strategy can be used to minimize the chance of meeting the watch
captain's potential wand of fire/cold/death.


